(* Linear Search: Sequentially examines each array element from index 0 to N-1 until) Tj
T*
(target is matched. Time complexity: Best Case O\(1\), Worst Case O\(N\), Average Case) Tj
T*
(O\(N\). Applicable to unsorted arrays.) Tj
T*
(* Binary Search: Divide-and-conquer search on sorted arrays. Compares target with) Tj
T*
(middle element mid = low + \(high - low\)/2. If target < arr[mid], search left half; if) Tj
T*
(target > arr[mid], search right half. Time complexity: Best Case O\(1\), Worst/Average) Tj
T*
(Case O\(log2 N\). Space complexity: O\(1\) iterative.) Tj
