(>> 4.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Derive physical memory address mapping formula for a 2D array in Row-Major) Tj
T*
(Order vs. Column-Major Order.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Let a 2D array be declared as A[M][N] with base address B and element size S) Tj
T*
(bytes. \(1\) Row-Major Order: Elements of Row 0 stored contiguously, followed by Row 1, up) Tj
T*
(to Row M-1. To access element A[i][j], program skips 'i' complete rows of N elements) Tj
T*
(each, plus 'j' elements within row i. Address\(A[i][j]\) = B + [ i * N + j ] * S. \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Column-Major Order: Elements of Column 0 stored contiguously, followed by Column 1, up) Tj
T*
(to Column N-1. To access A[i][j], program skips 'j' complete columns of M elements each,) Tj
T*
(plus 'i' elements within column j. Address\(A[i][j]\) = B + [ j * M + i ] * S.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain why Binary Search cannot be applied to an unsorted array, and derive) Tj
T*
(its worst-case time complexity.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Binary Search relies strictly on monotonicity \(ordered property\) of data. It) Tj
T*
(assumes that if target key > arr[mid], target CANNOT exist in left half [low, mid-1],) Tj
T*
(safely discarding N/2 elements in a single comparison. In an unsorted array, this) Tj
T*
(assumption fails because larger elements could reside anywhere. Derivation of Time) Tj
T*
(Complexity: At each step, search space is divided by 2. After step 1: N/2; step 2: N/4;) Tj
T*
(step k: N / 2^k. Search terminates when 1 element remains: N / 2^k = 1 => 2^k = N => k =) Tj
T*
(log2\(N\). Therefore, worst-case number of comparisons is proportional to log2\(N\), giving) Tj
T*
(O\(log N\) time complexity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.5 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Arrays allocate contiguous physical memory; 2D arrays in C use Row-Major order.) Tj
T*
(* Linear search is O\(N\); Binary search achieves O\(log N\) on pre-sorted arrays.) Tj
T*
(* Bubble sort is stable with O\(N^2\) complexity \(optimizable to O\(N\) using a swap) Tj
T*
(flag\).) Tj
T*
(* Matrix multiplication of \(m x p\) and \(p x n\) requires O\(m * p * n\) operations.) Tj
T*
